'''''[[Altolamprologus compressiceps]]''''' is a species of fish in the family [[Cichlid]]ae, endemic to the shallow rocky areas of [[Lake Tanganyika]]. The lake holds at least 250 species of cichlid fish, including species yet to be described. Almost all (98 percent) of Tanganyika cichlid species are [[Endemism|endemic]] to the lake, and it is thus an important biological resource for the study of [[speciation]] in evolution. ''A.&nbsp;compressiceps'' is categorized as a [[least-concern species]] by the [[International Union for Conservation of Nature]]. This fish was photographed at the [[Karlsruhe Zoo]] in Germany.

